# Design: TLA+ execution transition model

## Problem
Task T015 will implement the Rust run-state validation. The state rules
for queues, retries, cancellation, and late results needed a checked
model first, as AGENTS.md section 7 requires.

## Approach
One model of one run. Transition guards express the Rust state
boundary. TLC explored two bounded configurations to completion. A
mutant that stores an offered binding on retry violates
AttemptBindingStable, so the invariants detect drift.

## Key Trade-offs
- The pending limit counts never-started work only. A retry keeps its
  queue slot, because in-flight work is not new work. T030 and T032
  must implement this rule.
- The binding is two string identity fields. TLC refuses equality
  between a string and a tuple, so a pair of fields replaces one
  composite value.
- Refused events are a counter with a cap of three. This keeps the
  reachable state set finite. The record states the omission.
- Time is one Cancel or Deadline event. Backoff durations and attempt
  budgets stay outside the model.
- TLC runs outside the ordinary suite, because the jar is not part of
  the repository. A repo check keeps the record matching the module.

